      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Using hydrogen peroxide is outdated; it can actually damage healthy tissue, and superglue is not a sterile medical closing agent for a puncture wound. For a deep, dirty puncture, the real danger is infection, which requires professional cleaning and possibly a tetanus shot. Since you need it to heal, I strongly advise you to seek professional care to prevent serious complications.",
      "source": "target",
