      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Soaking it in a strong antiseptic is better than peroxide, but it won't disinfect deep puncture wounds effectively. Apply a thick layer of an antibiotic ointment, cover it with a sterile, non-stick dressing, and change the dressing several times a day. If you notice any increasing redness, swelling, throbbing pain, or pus, you must stop working and see a doctor immediately.",
      "source": "target",
